n-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 377474, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WkYkqJ23Jd5AsFypx7Go82", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377474, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WkYkqJ23Jd5AsFypx7Go82", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381645, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212). So `2.665` rounded to `2.67`, but the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 with the advisory tool, but it isn't in the advisory database. It's probably an internal ticket ID, not a security advisory, and the fix didn't depend on it. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CV8Q3AcnVUDTT6a616Dn5T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013ERvAbvSgdtHpvoier5sCi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UdvSy92xD6vGBCqSVBg4JF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input