F_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nChange: `round_money` now quantizes with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212). So `2.665` rounded to `2.67`, but the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 with the advisory tool, but it isn't in the advisory database. It's probably an internal ticket ID, not a security advisory, and the fix didn't depend on it. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}